1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,104
Question one.

2
00:00:01,104 --> 00:00:07,050
Step one: macro scan. It asks what these raw readings are best called.

3
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:10,363
One mark. Command words: “best called”.

4
00:00:10,363 --> 00:00:11,892
Step two: denoise.

5
00:00:11,892 --> 00:00:14,610
Useful, in yellow: raw readings.

6
00:00:14,610 --> 00:00:18,687
In cyan: “not yet” turned into charts or alerts.

7
00:00:18,687 --> 00:00:24,887
Useless red herring: rural site, every hour, which sensors — kick it out.

8
00:00:24,887 --> 00:00:26,416
Step three: draft.

9
00:00:26,416 --> 00:00:29,049
Raw and unprocessed means data.

10
00:00:29,049 --> 00:00:32,702
Processed and meaningful means information.

11
00:00:32,702 --> 00:00:34,995
“Not yet” keeps it at data.

12
00:00:34,995 --> 00:00:36,439
Step four: P O E.

13
00:00:36,439 --> 00:00:41,875
B, information: already processed, clashes with “not yet” — cut.

14
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:44,848
C, knowledge: level too high — cut.

15
00:00:44,848 --> 00:00:47,311
D, wisdom: even higher — cut.

16
00:00:47,311 --> 00:00:55,211
Step five: sanity check and lock. What is left is uninterpreted raw fact, matching “not yet”.

17
00:00:55,211 --> 00:00:57,504
So the correct answer is A.

